# Checkouts are LF, everywhere, on every machine.
#
# Several build-time gates read text files as bytes: the alpha-shell recipe refuses a file that is
# not LF-terminated, and the materials digests in `crates/voxel-model/materials/digest.txt` are
# hashes of the files themselves. `core.autocrlf=true` is set system-wide on Windows, so without a
# policy a checkout on a Windows runner rewrote them to CRLF and those gates refused a tree that was
# correct as committed. `eol=lf` makes the bytes a build sees the bytes that were committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The exceptions: files whose committed bytes are *not* LF, and which a build hashes verbatim.
# `-text` turns off every conversion in both directions, so what was recorded stays what is read.
# The SPLIB07A spectra are distributed as CRLF (and `sources.tsv` is a mix of both), and the two
# generated modules were recorded with CRLF line endings.
crates/voxel-model/materials/** -text
crates/voxel-model/src/materials/generated.rs -text
crates/voxel-model/src/materials/spectra.rs -text
